# Working with dude

[`dude`](https://github.com/cubocicloide/dude) is the project CLI — a single
entry point for all development tasks. Run `dude help` for a live overview, and
`dude help <command>` (or `dude help <group> <sub>`) for a command's flags.

---

## Installation

`dude` is published on the public npm registry. What you install
globally is the tiny **launcher** (`@cubocicloide/dude-launcher`); it then runs
each project's *pinned* CLI + stack automatically — no manual version switching.

```bash
# 1. Install the launcher globally (the only global install).
npm install -g @cubocicloide/dude-launcher
```

Then, inside this project, provision the pinned toolchain (the launcher would
also do this on the first `dude` command, but doing it explicitly is clearer):

```bash
pnpm install      # installs the pinned @cubocicloide/dude CLI + stack
dude version      # verify the resolved CLI + stack versions
```


