## Getting started

### First run

```bash
# Build images and start all services — required the very first time
dude up
```

From the second run onward:

```bash
dude up
```

Also re-run `dude up --build` whenever you change a `Dockerfile` or
`pyproject.toml`.

### Services

Once the stack is up, open these URLs:

| Service | URL | Notes |
|---------|-----|-------|
| **Frontend** | http://localhost:5173 | React + Vite — HMR active |
| **API** | http://localhost:8000 | Django REST Framework |
| **API reference** | http://localhost:8000/api/docs/ | Interactive reference (Scalar) |
| **OpenAPI schema** | http://localhost:8000/api/schema/ | Raw schema (YAML, drf-spectacular) |
| **Health** | http://localhost:8000/api/health/ | JSON health check |
| **Django admin** | http://localhost:8000/admin/ | Themed by [Unfold](https://unfoldadmin.com); create an account with `dude db superuser` |
{{#if withS3}}| **MinIO console** | http://localhost:9001 | Object-storage UI (minioadmin/minioadmin) |
{{/if}}
{{#if withCelery}}| **Flower** | http://localhost:5555 | Celery task monitor |
{{/if}}

### Hot reload

- **Frontend** — Vite HMR is active. Edit any file under `frontend/src/` and
  the browser updates instantly without a full page reload.
- **Backend** — Django's development server auto-reloads. Edit any Python file
  under `backend/apps/` or `backend/config/` and the API restarts within ~1
  second. Migrations run automatically when the container boots (`start.sh`).

