## Database (migrations)

Schema changes are managed with Django migrations. These commands run inside
the backend container.

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `dude db makemigration [--app <app>] [--name <text>]` | Autogenerate a migration from model changes |
| `dude db migrate` | Apply all pending migrations |
| `dude db migrate --app <app> --revision <rev>` | Migrate one app to a specific migration |
| `dude db rollback --app <app> --to <rev>` | Roll one app back (`--to zero` reverts it fully) |
| `dude db superuser` | Create a Django admin account (interactive) |

**Workflow** — after changing a model:

```bash
dude db makemigration --app users --name "add nickname"
dude db migrate
git add backend/apps/users/migrations/
```

